# DSP (two DSP48E2 sites): a tile type the reference never fuzzed; its window
# is in tilegrid.windows. Generated by designs/kv260_dsp_char/emit_dsp.py
# from that directory's random specimens (32 DSP48E2s each, every attribute
# and control-pin tie random; build2, DATA_TIES=1, ties the data buses too).
# The features are the effective ones nextpnr writes (write_dsp_usp), with
# Vivado's normalisation applied; see emit_dsp.py's docstring for each. With
# them, every tile instance of every specimen is predicted exactly (no bit
# missing, none extra). D_TIE1 has no bits for D[3], D[13] and D[23].
# OUT_ROW<r> are tile features: INT row r carries a used output
# (designs/kv260_dsp_char/out_rows.txt, from a single-pin specimen).
# Regenerate:
#   emit_dsp.py build build2 --emit x && (cat header; cat x) > this file
